  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 removes any automatic sales ban for models above 5% (the threshold now only triggers regulator review and corrective action), which protects Northwind's 6.2% Hearth 10 and is the main gain for Northwind. S3 gives installed units a 6-year retrofit window, and S5 imposes a mandatory recall at 8 per 100k with no transition, which would capture Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. The new-unit shut-off date is given as a calendar date (1 January 2029) with no adoption date, so its months-from-adoption value is left null."
